        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T14:15:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unless it leads to an avalanche of trouble, I feel like the cleaner fix would be to take a `size_t` in `Vec::operator[]` instead of an int.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 620,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 620,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "e1017746692e9ef9d1fcbd6f96b69826beca6099",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9469b8aa_edda98a8",
        "filename": "include/private/SkVx.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 620,
      "author": {
        "id": 5210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T21:57:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I don\u0027t want to mess with this right now. It is template hell. But, I actually prefer operator[int]. For Skia, it makes more sense. Skia is kind of int based.",
      "parentUuid": "cce4b2cf_fd16b657",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 620,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 620,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "e1017746692e9ef9d1fcbd6f96b69826beca6099",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9a5e3ac8_07c5112e",
        "filename": "include/private/SkVx.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 620,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-24T13:47:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Let\u0027s add a TODO to look at fixing the `operator[]`.\n\nPersonally I don\u0027t think Skia is anything-based, there\u0027s too many containers and pieces written by different people at different times with different ideas. Some parts are int-based; others not at all. (e.g. the part I know the most clearly, SkSL, has never been int-centric since it grew up around the STL)",
      "parentUuid": "9469b8aa_edda98a8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 620,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 620,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "e1017746692e9ef9d1fcbd6f96b69826beca6099",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0226d29e_81e3a15a",
        "filename": "include/private/SkVx.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 620,
      "author": {
        "id": 5210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-24T14:08:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that SKSL is the only piece of Skia that is not int-centric, and that heavily uses the STL.",
      "parentUuid": "9a5e3ac8_07c5112e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 620,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 620,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "e1017746692e9ef9d1fcbd6f96b69826beca6099",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "964f843d_bac6a84c",
        "filename": "src/core/SkGlyphBuffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 223,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T14:15:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Without reviewing all of the code in the class, changing an unsigned type to a signed type could be risky. (Various operations are defined for unsigned types but UB for a signed type.) WDYT about using uint32_t?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 223,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 223,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "e1017746692e9ef9d1fcbd6f96b69826beca6099",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4e1f45ab_1c0f2aaf",
        "filename": "src/core/SkGlyphBuffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 223,
      "author": {
        "id": 5210
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T21:57:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wrote this class, I\u0027m pretty comfortable with this. The largest number of glyphs is 2^20. This seems fine, and I invite the UB warning because they would have been errors.",
      "parentUuid": "964f843d_bac6a84c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 223,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 223,
        "endChar": 7
      },
      "revId": "e1017746692e9ef9d1fcbd6f96b69826beca6099",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f39b99b9_1efa7cfd",
        "filename": "src/core/SkGlyphBuffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 223,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-24T13:47:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "UB warnings are the good case. The real concern is introducing new unwarned UB, e.g. wraparound for unsigned is defined; wraparound for signed is not. We might be able to catch this sort of thing with fuzzers + UBSAN but I don\u0027t know how likely that is.",
      "parentUuid": "4e1f45ab_1c0f2aaf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 223,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 223,
        "endChar": 7
